<speak>
<s>This is your Jumu'ah briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">05062026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Japan's trade ministry has proposed building fourteen new nuclear reactors at existing plant sites — the clearest reversal yet of the retreat that followed Fukushima.</s> <s>After the twenty-eleven disaster, Japan shut all fifty-four of its reactors, and today imported fuel covers up to seventy percent of its power as demand from artificial intelligence climbs.</s> <s>Building on old sites sidesteps years of siting fights... but whether a wary public accepts it is the open question.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Chinese leader Xi Jinping will travel to Pyongyang on the eighth and ninth of June — a state visit so rare it amounts to a statement in itself.</s> <s>Chinese leaders almost never go to North Korea, and the trip signals how far the alignment between Beijing, Moscow and Pyongyang has hardened against Washington.</s> <s>No agenda's been announced, and the joint statement afterward will reveal just how deep the bloc now runs.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Peru, just six-tenths of a point separate the two candidates heading into the presidential runoff.</s> <s>Leftist Sanchez, an ally of jailed former president Pedro Castillo, leads Keiko Fujimori — daughter of an imprisoned authoritarian — within the margin of error, an Ipsos poll found.</s> <s>Publishing polls is banned in the final week, and thirteen percent of voters remain undecided, enough to tip a decade of instability either way.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>For Egypt's former political prisoners, release rarely means freedom.</s> <s>The Al-Nadeem Center documented three hundred and nine forced disappearances last year and seventy-eight deaths in custody, with freed detainees re-arrested in fresh cases it calls recycling.</s> <s>Three rights defenders who exposed that pattern were themselves arrested, and no law limits how often a person can be pulled back in.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Iraqi Kurdistan, a long-promised plan to merge two rival armies into one national force is collapsing.</s> <s>The Kurdistan Democratic Party and the Patriotic Union each still command their own troops, and a US-backed reform deal will expire in September unfinished.</s> <s>As long as two ruling families each hold their own soldiers, the region keeps no single monopoly on force, leaving it exposed to Baghdad, Ankara and Tehran alike.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Ukraine's President Zelensky has publicly dared Vladimir Putin to meet him face to face, proposing Turkey or Arab states as hosts.</s> <s>The open letter signals a shift toward regional mediators as American attention stays fixed on Iran.</s> <s>Putin's already questioned Zelensky's legitimacy as a negotiating partner, and a public dare is not yet a negotiation.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In South Africa, half of all commercial-crime cases drag through fourteen postponements before they're heard.</s> <s>Cases collapse through withdrawals and delays rather than weak evidence — thirty-four percent are simply dropped, a University of Cape Town study found.</s> <s>Prosecutors dispute the method, but a justice system that runs out of patience lets white-collar power outlast accountability.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Bangladesh's only nuclear plant, Rooppur, has tied Dhaka to Moscow for decades to come.</s> <s>Russia provided the loans, the engineers and the fuel, and it retains control of all three, with no alternative supplier or spare-parts chain in sight.</s> <s>A single megaproject has quietly converted into multi-decade strategic capture, and an energy bet may have mortgaged a nation's foreign-policy autonomy.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India's Tata Motors is aiming for more than a fifth of a passenger-vehicle market it expects to reach six million cars a year by twenty thirty.</s> <s>Tata already holds forty percent of India's electric-vehicle sales and has committed thirty-five thousand crore rupees in fresh investment, its chairman said.</s> <s>The target is really a claim on who controls India's electrified future — a domestic champion, or the global automakers it hopes to hold off.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nigeria's Dangote refinery has pushed past its design capacity to seven hundred thousand barrels a day.</s> <s>For decades the country exported crude and imported refined fuel, yet now Dangote ships jet fuel to Europe, the United States and Saudi Arabia, <sub alias="S and P Global">S&P Global</sub> data shows.</s> <s>A continent long defined as a raw-materials exporter is watching one plant rewrite that story.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Two of the newest Omicron lineages, including the strain called <sub alias="J N one">JN.1</sub>, have gained the ability to infect upper-intestinal tissue that earlier variants couldn't reach.</s> <s>Using the same cell-surface receptors earlier strains relied on, they colonise the gut with little inflammation, a new study found.</s> <s>As the virus drifts, it isn't only dodging immunity — it's widening which organs it can occupy, raising the prospect of silent shedding long after a pandemic feels over.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>After a search lasting nearly a decade, a team in Taiwan has crowned a giant cypress nicknamed Heaven Sword as East Asia's tallest known tree.</s> <s>Climbers, ecologists and remote-sensing specialists combed the island's rugged interior since twenty fourteen for any specimen over eighty metres.</s> <s>Most of Earth's tallest living things remain unmapped, and finding these giants meant fusing laser mapping with old-fashioned rope and nerve.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Deep in the Irminger Basin, researchers have identified an entirely new family of copepods, two and a half thousand metres down.</s> <s>Copepods are the most abundant animals in the ocean, yet finding a new family — not just a species — fills a real gap in a poorly understood branch of the tree of life.</s> <s>That basin has been sampled in only a handful of expeditions, a reminder of how little of the deep sea we've actually seen.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Microsoft's chief executive Satya Nadella has publicly distanced himself from his own company's leaked ambition to make its AI products addictive.</s> <s>An internal document by a company vice-president listed making people addicted as a first-phase goal, and Nadella told staff he didn't know who wrote it.</s> <s>When the engagement logic that hollowed out social media gets ported to AI assistants, the tell isn't one rogue author — it's that no one's withdrawn the plan.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Uber has capped each engineer's spending on AI coding tools at fifteen hundred dollars a month, after burning through its annual budget by April.</s> <s>That ceiling runs to about eleven percent of a median American software engineer's yearly pay — an accidental disclosure of what heavy AI use really costs.</s> <s>The cheap-assistant story hides per-seat costs that flat subscription pricing can't sustain, and the subsidised era of these tools may be ending.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A lawsuit has exposed a Palantir system that scores immigrants' addresses to flag entire neighbourhoods for deportation targeting.</s> <s>Just Futures Law sued US Immigration and Customs Enforcement for records on the tool, even as a Palantir executive is reportedly in line to lead the federal agency that guards critical infrastructure.</s> <s>A firm that sells data-fusion tools to the government may soon be helping run it — the revolving door at its starkest.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>